      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good catch! I wasn\u0027t seeing this in viewer at first because of the default 2x hi-dpi scale factor, but at 1x, these round rects had fractional coords of `2/3`. \n\nWith the original hairline snapping code I wrote, this would round the left and top edges up to the next integer and then we\u0027d inset 1/2px from there. All the other backends, and the equivalent behavior for a non-hairline 1px stroke with identity scale, would be to outset by 1/2, then round, and then inset again by 1/2. In that case, the outset fraction becomes less than 1/2 and rounds down.\n\nWith that implemented for hairline strokes, I am now seeing the complexclip2_rrect case aligning exactly with the raster backend whereas previously the top and left edges were in by one pixel.",
      "parentUuid": "c108f426_fe8b52c0",
      "revId": "3ec4e4dfa0f98fd58e9582dc2ba4c955d0d77ad5",
